Wait — there's an issue with the hour wraparound: (9 + i*2) % 24 for i up to 19 → 9+38=47 %24 = 23; sequence: 9,11,13,15,17,19,21,23,1,3,... The end hour (10+i*2)%24 follows start+1 mod 24 — when start=23, end=0 → end "00:00" same day → end < start → create fails with 422! i=7: start=(9+14)%24=23, end=(10+14)%24=0 → invalid. Fix: compute instants from a base Instant plus hours instead of formatting. Better: 

```java
Instant startInstant = Instant.parse("2026-10-04T09:00:00Z").plusSeconds(i * 7200L);
String start = startInstant.toString();
String end = startInstant.plusSeconds(3600).toString();
```

